Subject: [PATCH] GuiMenu: hide the ZRAM SWAP menu on RK3128

The menu knows lz4 or lz4 + zstd recompression and sizes of 50-150 % of
RAM. The Powkiddy A12 runs a measured lzo-rle zram with zstd
recompression of idle pages at a fixed 256 MB: the menu shows its zstd
switch off and its size as 100 %, and any change replaces that tuning.
Leave the entry out on RK3128 (ES builds with -D$DEVICE).

--- a/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp
@@ -2272,7 +2272,11 @@
 		});
 	}
 
+#if !defined(RK3128)
+	// The A12 runs a measured lzo-rle + zstd-recompress zram at a fixed size,
+	// which this menu can neither show nor keep.
 	s->addEntry(_("ZRAM SWAP"), true, [this] { openZramSettings(); });
+#endif
 
 #if defined(SM6115)
 	// Add option to set gpu max clock speed
